{"name":"Red Wire","hex":"#db5947","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"wire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Metal formed into a thin, even thread, now usually by being drawn through a hole in a steel die.","A piece of such material; a thread or slender rod of metal, a cable."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten with wire, especially with reference to wine bottles, corks, or fencing.","To string on a wire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wire","blocks":[{"text":"A wire is a flexible, round bar of metal. Wires are commonly formed by drawing the metal through a hole in a die or draw plate. Wire gauges come in various standard sizes, as expressed in terms of a gauge number or cross-sectional area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Sample_cross-section_of_high_tension_power_%28pylon%29_line.jpg/330px-Sample_cross-section_of_high_tension_power_%28pylon%29_line.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wire","wikidata":"Q551997"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Wire_wrapped_jewelry.JPG/500px-Wire_wrapped_jewelry.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Wire_wrapped_jewelry.JPG/1280px-Wire_wrapped_jewelry.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Wire_wrapped_jewelry.JPG/500px-Wire_wrapped_jewelry.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wire wrapped jewelry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWire_wrapped_jewelry.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Sophie_Ryder%27s_%22Sitting%22_%28side_view%29.jpg/500px-Sophie_Ryder%27s_%22Sitting%22_%28side_view%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Sophie_Ryder%27s_%22Sitting%22_%28side_view%29.jpg/1280px-Sophie_Ryder%27s_%22Sitting%22_%28side_view%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Sophie_Ryder%27s_%22Sitting%22_%28side_view%29.jpg/500px-Sophie_Ryder%27s_%22Sitting%22_%28side_view%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sophie Ryder's galvanised wire sculpture Sitting at the Yorkshire Sculpture Park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/